# YouTube Music provider

This optional native plugin adapts guest catalog and playback integration from MetroList at commit `e97197786c2a7ad56279cc9bb4ce3233ef6c99ff`. It registers through the public MetroFuse plugin SDK and owns its unauthenticated network session. The plugin code is GPL-3.0. The build bundles [InnerTubeX v0.11.7](https://github.com/MetrolistGroup/innertubex/tree/v0.11.7) and its [QuackJS v0.1.4](https://github.com/MetrolistGroup/quackjs/tree/v0.1.4) dependency. The packaged license is the one in the repository root. Kotlin, the application's Ktor runtime/HTTP engine, Compose and the MetroFuse API are supplied by the application. The plugin constructs an isolated `HttpClient` with Ktor's default engine discovery: it does not reference desktop-only CIO classes on Android.

Build with `gradlew -PbuildYoutubeMusicPlugin=true :plugin-youtube-music:packagePluginJar :plugin-youtube-music:packagePluginApk --no-configuration-cache`. Outputs go to `plugins/providers/youtube-music/build/outputs/plugins/`. Import the JAR on Windows or the APK in MetroFuse on Android, then enable it. Search, catalog and metadata use the public guest session. Audio can be switched off in plugin settings. Guest stream resolution depends on service availability and the host's provider timeout. Account features, SABR and music videos are outside this plugin's scope.

The build stamps the native manifest's Compose ABI from the repository's pinned Kotlin/Compose versions. APK packaging converts the provider and Android dependency classes with D8 and preserves dependency assets and any JNI libraries. QuackJS 0.1.4 is Kotlin-only; its published Android AAR contains no JNI binaries. Host Kotlin, coroutines, serialization and Ktor classes are compile-only and are not embedded in the plugin.

Catalog tracks retain provider album links. Playlist parsing preserves repeated track occurrences. The native client derives content locale from the operating system; it does not inherit the application's YouTube account. Only the first browse/search page is currently exposed. Full continuation loading and account parity are unimplemented.

A separate universal JavaScript implementation lives in `../youtube-music-js`. It contains its own public catalog/direct-audio resolver and a limited signature interpreter. It does not wrap the native JAR or APK. All variants share the same plugin owner; import one implementation at a time. Parser, packaging and lifecycle fixtures do not prove live service/CDN playback.

The guest catalog discovers the current WEB_REMIX client version from the public YouTube Music `sw.js_data` bootstrap. Locale is derived from the system; the bootstrap is bounded in size and cached per plugin activation.
